#!/bin/sh
# Non-blocking reminder printed after every commit. It never fails the commit —
# it just drops the repo's commit-message convention into the terminal (and thus
# into an agent's context) so the next commit trends back toward the house style.
#
# Only shown when stderr isn't a TTY, i.e. an agent/tool commit rather than a
# human committing interactively at a terminal.
#
# Enable once per clone with:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks

[ -t 2 ] && exit 0

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

Commit style reminder: a short imperative subject, then a paragraph or two of prose
explaining the intent of the change, no tautology repeating what the code does, nor
self-talk about how the conversation went.
`git commit --amend` if needed.

EOF
